; NextDAAD 256-colour text fixture.
;
; Compiled by tests\build-tests.ps1 on every run and asserted at the
; byte level there; staged as the active GAME.DDB in sd\PALETTE\ by
; tests\build-tests.ps1 -Palette.
;
; WHAT IT PINS
; DRC declares INK, PAPER and BORDER as a single generic value
; parameter checked only against 0-255, so a value above 15 is
; expressible in the database today. This fixture authors such values
; and the harness asserts the exact bytes reached the DDB, so a future
; toolchain change that starts folding them is caught immediately.
;
; LOOK prints one line in each of four extended combinations, then a
; 16-colour block that must still render exactly as it did before the
; 256-colour work. EXAMINE walks 32 ink values against one paper, which
; is the pair allocator's pressure test.
;
; THE LAYER 2 CARD. 001.NXI is the 256x128 full-colour reference card
; tests\art\mkpalcard.py generates: a 16 x 16 grid of every palette
; index in order, on the identity palette, so swatch n is the same
; colour INK n produces. It sits above the text deliberately - reading
; a text line against the swatch of the same number is what turns "that
; looks about right" into an actual check, and it puts Layer 2 and the
; tilemap on screen together so interference between them would show.
; Swatch 255, bottom right, is a hole rather than a colour: 255 is the
; reserved transparent index, so the text layer shows through it.
;
; THE RED BACKDROP IS WHAT MAKES THE HOLE READABLE. Before the card is
; drawn, the window is shaped to the card's own footprint - rows 4 to
; 19, columns 8 to 71, exactly the area 256x128 art covers - and cleared
; to paper 224, a saturated red. The card then covers every cell of it
; except swatch 255. So red showing at row 19, columns 68 to 71 is
; transparency working, and black there is transparency failing. Without
; a backdrop the hole reveals the tilemap's own default black paper and
; a working hole is indistinguishable from a broken one, which is
; exactly the trap tests\art\mkl2card.py's header warns about.
;
; WINDOW LAYOUT. 256-wide art is top-aligned and the screen below stays
; transparent (manual\graphics.md), so the card covers tilemap rows 4 to
; 19 and the text window opens at row 20 with 12 rows. The More... pager
; is left ON: the pressure block prints 200 cells into 12 rows, so it
; pages, and stepping through it a screen at a time is how the eviction
; behaviour is actually read.
;
; PICTURE IS A CONDITION, so a card that fails to load aborts its entry
; and the colour text still prints from the entry after it. A run with
; no art is a visibly degraded fixture rather than a blank screen.

/CTL
_
/VOC
LOOK   4  verb
EXAMINE 5 verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key."
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
